    "explanation": "1. P1 (test imp=None) runs improve_dt(n_sweeps=0, repair=True) after gmsh is finalized with default project='planar', which locks every cylinder-wall and rim-circle node (r=a). In wave-3 (split_projector=None), all fixing flips and boundary-edge Steiner splits on the negative faces are refused with 'locked'. 2. P3 (repair_study.py flip-only) calls flip_to_delaunay(m, mats) with locked=None (no nodes locked), so wave-3 bnd_edge Steiner mode split boundary edges at their chord midpoints (recorded in results/repair.json: {'flips': {'2-3': 4, '3-2': 0, '4-4': 0, '2-2': 0}, 'steiner_nodes': 2, 'refused': {'boundary': 3}, 'negative_faces_before': 2, 'negative_faces_after': 0, 'stuck': []}), placing Steiner nodes on the chord off the curved cylinder wall. 3. P2 (imp=True) and P4 (study improve) run inside mesh_cad with cad_projector, which lets smooth cylinder-wall surface nodes slide (locked=False) and locks only the 1D CAD rim circles. With CadSplitProjector and feature_curve_projector, locked rim and curved-wall edges are split and projected onto the CAD curve/surface while unprojected chord splits on curved boundaries are refused with 'no_projector'."
